description: Kotlin Multiplatform rules for shared, core, and feature modules. Use when editing Kotlin under shared/, core/, or feature/.
globs: shared/**/*.kt,core/**/*.kt,feature/**/*.kt
alwaysApply: false
---

# KMP shared

- Package root is `com.mvpmodular`. Match the Gradle path: `com.mvpmodular.feature.auth.api`, `com.mvpmodular.core.network`.
- `:feature:<name>:api` holds models, repository interfaces, and use cases. Use cases return `Outcome<T, DomainError>`.
- `:feature:<name>:impl` holds the repository, platform `actual`s, `UiState`, `ViewModel`, and `val <name>Module`. Repository and gateway classes are `internal`.
- An impl depends on its own api, on other features' api modules, and on `:core:*`. It does not depend on another impl.
- An api depends only on `:core:common` and other feature apis. It does not touch Ktor, SQL, or Koin.
- Do not add `ServiceLoader`, classpath scanning, or dynamic feature delivery. Register Koin modules in `featureModules()` in `shared`.
- Feature flags gate behavior inside an already-linked use case. They do not load code.
- HTTP goes through `BffClient`. Platform engines stay in `androidMain` / `iosMain`.
- Keep `expect`/`actual` for platform SDKs (billing, push, HTTP engine). iOS actuals exist even though Linux does not compile them.
- Nested modules must keep a unique Gradle `group` (`com.mvpmodular.` + project path) and the path-based Kotlin module name from `mvp.kmp.library`. Do not set `group = "com.mvpmodular"` again.
- New feature: follow the `new-feature-module` skill, including `settings.gradle.kts`, `AppBootstrap`, `SharedGraph`, and the `export` list in `mvp.kmp.shared.gradle.kts`.
